          up: {"title":"ITQ2 in action: the term grade book (Challenge)","intro":"<p>The Form 5 year head needs a grade book for 120 students in 8 subjects, ready for parents' evening. Some choices are reasonable but not the best. Choose the BEST option each time.</p>","nodes":{"start":{"text":"<p>Which software should hold the grade book?</p>","choices":[{"t":"A spreadsheet, because 960 marks must be totalled, averaged and recalculated whenever one is corrected.","to":"n2","fb":"Right. Calculation and automatic recalculation are the deciding factors."},{"t":"A word processor table, because it prints neatly.","to":"bad1","fb":"A table in a word processor cannot recalculate averages when a mark changes."},{"t":"A database, because there are 120 student records.","to":"ok1","fb":"A database can store the records, but the job here is mainly calculation and recalculation, which a spreadsheet does more simply."}]},"n2":{"text":"<p>Eight teachers will type their own marks. Last term someone typed 840 instead of 84, and another typed 77O with a letter O. What do you add?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Data validation on the mark cells: whole numbers from 0 to 100 only, with an error alert.","to":"n3","fb":"Excellent. The impossible entries are rejected before they can spoil any average."},{"t":"Conditional formatting that colours any mark above 100 red.","to":"ok2","fb":"It would show the problem, but only after the wrong mark is in and the averages are already wrong."},{"t":"Lock the sheet so that only the year head can type marks.","to":"bad2","fb":"This moves 960 entries onto one person and does not stop typing errors."}]},"n3":{"text":"<p>Each student's average is in column J. The year head wants column K to show \"Pass\" for 50 or more and \"Fail\" otherwise. Which formula goes in K2?</p>","choices":[{"t":"=IF(J2>50,\"Pass\",\"Fail\")","to":"bad3","fb":"A student with an average of exactly 50 would wrongly show \"Fail\"."},{"t":"Type Pass or Fail by hand for each student.","to":"ok3","fb":"It works today, but it will not update when a mark is corrected."},{"t":"=IF(J2>=50,\"Pass\",\"Fail\")","to":"n4","fb":"Correct, and >= includes a student on exactly 50."}]},"n4":{"text":"<p>For parents' evening, the year head wants at-risk students to stand out AND a summary of how many students passed in each class. What do you set up?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Ask a student helper to highlight weak averages by hand.","to":"bad4","fb":"Slow, error-prone, and out of date after the next correction."},{"t":"Conditional formatting that shades averages below 50 red, plus a PivotTable that counts Pass and Fail by class.","to":"good","fb":"Excellent. One feature highlights individuals; the other summarises the whole year group."},{"t":"Sort the whole sheet by average and print it.","to":"ok4","fb":"The weakest students rise to the top, but the class summary is missing and the list must be re-sorted after every correction."}]},"good":{"text":"<p><b>Grade One set-up!</b> The grade book rejects impossible marks, calculates grades correctly at the boundary, highlights at-risk students and summarises passes by class, all updating automatically. Parents' evening runs smoothly.</p>","end":"good"},"ok1":{"text":"<p><b>Workable, but harder.</b> The records are stored safely, but building the averages and recalculations takes far longer than in a spreadsheet. Try again.</p>","end":"ok"},"ok2":{"text":"<p><b>Too late.</b> The red cell is spotted only after the class averages have been printed with the wrong mark included. Prevention beats detection. Try again.</p>","end":"ok"},"ok3":{"text":"<p><b>Out of date.</b> A corrected mark moves one student from 48 to 52, but the hand-typed \"Fail\" stays. Try again.</p>","end":"ok"},"ok4":{"text":"<p><b>Half the job.</b> The weak students are visible, but the year head still has to count passes for each class by hand. Try again.</p>","end":"ok"},"bad1":{"text":"<p><b>Wrong tool.</b> Every corrected mark means recalculating averages by hand. Try again.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad2":{"text":"<p><b>Bottleneck.</b> The year head spends three evenings typing marks and still makes errors. Try again.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad3":{"text":"<p><b>Boundary error.</b> Four students on exactly 50 are told they failed. Test the boundary in every IF formula. Try again.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad4":{"text":"<p><b>Missed students.</b> Two at-risk students are overlooked. Let the spreadsheet do the highlighting. Try again.</p>","end":"bad"}}}
